    "done_when": "reckon/velocity.py gains a report function. It takes a mapping of project name to checkout path, a window start and a window end, and returns compact_summary's shape, carrying every quantity the section's deliverable lists by project, by lane, by day, and in project-by-lane-by-day cells. It is composed from the existing capture_project, recover_ledger_clocks, measure and compact_summary, and none of their measurement logic is copied or re-implemented.\n\nreckon/mcp.py serves crew(view=\"velocity\"). It reads the existing since parameter as the window start and refuses by name when since is absent or unparseable. A new until parameter defaults to the current time. The view takes one project, or \"*\" for every mounted project, and resolves checkouts through the server's existing mount resolution. The response is compact_summary, never the commit census, so it stays within the transport bound. The view follows the pattern tests/test_crew_runs_view.py drives.\n\ntests/test_crew_velocity_view.py synthesises two git repositories with ledger rows under tmp_path, the way tests/test_velocity.py does, reads nothing outside tmp_path, and calls the view through the MCP function. It asserts:\n- the implementation-class and review-or-investigate promotion split and the review share on hand-computable fixtures;\n- one project-by-lane-by-day cell with its counts;\n- the refusal on a missing since;\n- that a commit dated after until is excluded.\n\nThat file, tests/test_velocity.py and tests/test_crew_runs_view.py pass at exit 0. The manifest records base and head arms over those three files in the armed JSON form with their FAILED ids, and the head arm runs at the committed head. The declared negative control is applied, the until case is observed to fail, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id. The reckon crew velocity command in reckon/cli.py is not part of this node, because a peer holds that file.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Serve the velocity view as crew(view=\"velocity\") for a window the caller names, through one report function in reckon/velocity.py that the later command-line surface will call unchanged",
